1. A computer-implemented method of displaying a stream of images on a display device, the method comprising, for each of a plurality of images of the stream:

- obtaining a predicted gaze point of a user on the display device;
- analysing image content of the image in a region associated with the predicted gaze point to determine a first display area around the predicted gaze point;
- assigning a first value of a display parameter to the first display area and assigning a second value of the display parameter, different from the first value, to at least one surrounding display area outside the first display area; and
- displaying the image on the display device such that the first display area is displayed in accordance with the first value of the display parameter and the at least one surrounding display area is displayed in accordance with the second value of the display parameter.
